<title>USA: Titan Wheel Int'l sells $150 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Titan Wheel Int'l sells $150 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Titan Wheel International Inc was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Titan Wheel International Inc is a global manufacturer of steel wheels and tires for off-highway vehicles used in the agricultural, consumer products, earthmoving/construction and</p>
<p>military markets.</p>
<p>BORROWER TITAN WHEEL INTERNATIONAL INC</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 8.75 PCT   MATURITY 4/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 99.50   FIRST PAY DATE 10/1/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B1    YIELD 8.825 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BB-MINUS  SPREAD 210 BPS    CALLABLE NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
